<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karaeng Pattingalloang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1600–1654</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karaeng Pattingalloang (1600–1654) was a nobleman of Tallo and chancellor of the twin kingdom of Gowa–Tallo in South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulawesi">Sulawesi</a> from 1639. Famous among European visitors for his learning, he read Portuguese and Spanish, collected European books and maps, and ordered a large globe from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>. He guided the policy of Makassar at the height of its power as a free trading port.</p></div>
